I generally start thinking of it as being mid-game when I start
spending more time on preparation for the future than on
immediate survival.  In the early game, you're mostly just
trying not to get killed right away.

There can be some exceptions, of course.  You might find
a general store on dungeon level three (which is obviously
early-game the first time you're there) and spend some time
(if you aren't actively starving) price-checking items, which
is preparation.  Going the other way, you can certainly get
into situations in the middle game where your life is in danger.

So the line between early game and mid-game is kind of blurry.
Nonetheless, I find it a useful distinction.

